  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 3347680,
  "published": "2026-11-27T14:19:53.73Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Initial public release.\n- Library view: library contents as table or inheritance tree, live search, selection synchronised with the AML tree.\n- Maintenance functions with undo/redo: sort A-Z, remove library, clean up empty elements, create attribute type library from untyped attributes, delete revision fields.\n- Excel export and import of libraries: attribute types, role classes, interface classes and SystemUnitClasses with name, version, parent, ID, description, semantic references and supported roles. Import checks that the sheet belongs to the open file and library (file name, library name, version, ID), matches entries by ID, shows all changes in a preview before applying, and keeps references valid when classes are renamed.\n- Migration: move references from old to new libraries, Auto Mapping (strict 1:1 or extended) with a reason per proposal, orphan detection, manual class search.\n- Split: one standalone AML file per library.\n- Compare: structural comparison with a second file - change list and side-by-side view, optional ID matching, version and SourceObjectInformation checks, jump to the element in the editor.\n- Health: live quality score against CAEX IEC 62424, AutomationML Edition 2 (IEC 62714-1) and the AML Library Development Guideline; findings, rule catalogue and statistics views; check mode with recommendations and strict rule check; Excel export of findings, rule violations and the rule catalogue.\n- Health repairs for typical defects, offered only when they occur: generate missing IDs, complete or set versions to the form a.b.c, correct SuperiorStandardVersion \"AutomationML 2.10\" to \"AutomationML 2.1\" - with undo/redo.\n- User interface in English (default) and German, switchable at any time.",
